      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nAdds MonkeyOCRv2 ([`zenosai/MonkeyOCRv2-B-Parsing`](https://huggingface.co/zenosai/MonkeyOCRv2-B-Parsing), about 265k downloads/month, # 1 open model on MDPBench, Apache-2.0). Today vLLM resolves it to `TransformersForCausalLM` and fails at startup (`Unrecognized configuration class MonkeyOCRv2Config ... for AutoModel`). No vLLM PR or issue covers it; the authors keep an out-of-tree copy of `dots_ocr.py` in their repo.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- The model is the dots.ocr vision encoder (768 wide, 12 layers) plus a Qwen3 language model. The one real difference is the axial RoPE layout: height and width frequencies are interleaved (`h0, w0, h1, w1, ...`) instead of concatenated.\r\n- `monkeyocr_v2.py` subclasses `DotsOCRForCausalLM` and overrides `rot_pos_emb`. Like `OpenCUAForConditionalGeneration`, it builds its own vision tower and language model (Qwen3) in `__init__`, so `dots_ocr.py` is unchanged. Processing reuses the Qwen2-VL path.\r\n- Registry, test registry and docs entries.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nCPU (Apple M5 Pro), fp32, greedy decoding, compared with the HF remote code:\r\n\r\n| Case | Prompt tokens | Tokens matching HF | Max \\|Δ logprob\\| |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| Text document | 691 | 57/57 (EOS) | 8.4e-4 |\r\n| Photo with text | 1445 | 64/64 | 5.7e-4 |\r\n| Both images in one prompt | 883 | 57/57 (EOS) | 8.5e-4 |\r\n\r\n- Batched and single requests give the same tokens.\r\n- With dots.ocr's RoPE layout instead, the document comes out as `1. 2. 3. ...`.\r\n- The HF reference needs one fix on Transformers 5: the remote vision tower's non-persistent `inv_freq` buffer loads as zeros.\r\n- `pytest tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_common.py -k \"MonkeyOCRv2 or dots.ocr\"`: 6 passed. Registry tests and pre-commit pass.\r\n- **Not validated:** CUDA, bf16, TP/PP, LoRA.\r\n\r\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
